top-level assertions (assertIsDisplayed/assertHasClickAction/onNodeWith*/performClick), mirroring the known-good
ServiceStatusUiTest. A whole-source-set compileDebugAndroidTestKotlin was run as an extra check: it fails ONLY
on pre-existing, out-of-scope sibling files (~24, e.g. EnergyStatsWidgetUiTest, KioskSettingsModal,
FSMStateDiagramUiTest, AnnotationListUiTest) that wrongly import assertDoesNotExist/assertExists/onAllNodes as
top-level symbols; ZERO errors mention CookieConsentBannerUiTest. Those files are outside this prompt's allowed
paths and were not modified (git status shows only the three new CookieConsentBanner directories).

Binding note: web CookieConsentBanner.tsx composes useVersionInfo().require_cookie_consent (the deployment GDPR
gate) with getConsent() (localStorage tri-state). The native surface binds the gate to the shared S8
SettingsStore.versionInfo() cache-then-network feed (the same useVersionInfo envelope the dashboard
VersionInfoWidget reads) and the per-user decision to a SharedPreferences-backed CookieConsentStore (the web
localStorage analogue, the TourLauncher precedent; key teslasync:consent:v1 reused verbatim). Where the web hides
itself with return null (loading / consent not needed / already decided), the surface renders every state as a
non-blank region per the platform contract (ServiceStatus precedent): loading skeleton, error+retry, the active
prompt (web's only rendered state), and a resolved recorded-state panel, plus orthogonal stale/offline chips.

